---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const description="Equal bodies forage, remember, leave fading traces, or pool their own observations. Food must survive the journey home.";
const path='/intelligence/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:"Roach Emergence",description,url:'https://iamrobin.ai'+path,learningResourceType:'Interactive simulation',inLanguage:'en'};
const content="<div class=\"swarm-lab\"><a class=\"lab-back\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/\">← Agent Swarm Lab</a><p class=\"lab-kicker\">Field study 01 / 06 · Roach Emergence</p><header class=\"lab-head\"><h1>Small minds.<br><em>Real dinner.</em></h1><p class=\"lab-deck\">A crowd is easy to animate. A useful crowd has to find something, carry it home, and pay for the journey.</p></header><p class=\"lab-zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">小小头脑，真正的晚餐。</p><section class=\"lab-stage\" data-swarm-model=\"/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/\" aria-label=\"Roach Emergence interactive simulator\">\n <div class=\"lab-stage-top\"><span><i class=\"lab-live-dot\"></i>OBSERVATORY / 01</span><span>Seeded simulation · evaluator view</span></div>\n <div class=\"lab-grid\"><div class=\"lab-view\"><canvas class=\"lab-world\" data-world aria-label=\"Animated orthographic 3D sketch of simulator states. Current and final measures are available in the table below.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-camera\"><button type=\"button\" data-camera>Plan / 3D</button><button type=\"button\" data-rotate>Rotate ↻</button></div></div>\n <aside class=\"lab-side\"><label>Treatment<select data-arm aria-label=\"Treatment\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-readout\"><strong data-live-value>—</strong><span data-live-label>Food delivered</span></div><p class=\"lab-event\" data-event>Observe. Compare. Change one assumption.</p><p class=\"small\">Lines = recorded movement / messages · cross = failed body.</p><div class=\"lab-checks\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-compare/>Compare all</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-trails checked/>Trails</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-signals checked/>Links</label></div><label>Inspect a body<select data-agent aria-label=\"Agent to inspect\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-inspect\" data-inspect><p class=\"small\">Click a body in the world, or choose it here. This is an evaluator view of recorded state.</p></div></aside></div>\n <div class=\"lab-buttons\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" data-play aria-pressed=\"false\">Play world</button><button type=\"button\" data-replay>Replay ↺</button><button type=\"button\" data-end>Final tick →</button><button type=\"button\" data-next-seed>Next seed</button><button type=\"button\" data-download>Save this run ↓</button></div>\n <label class=\"lab-timeline\"><span class=\"tiny\">Time</span><input data-timeline aria-label=\"Simulation timeline\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"0\"/><output data-time>0 ticks</output></label>\n <p class=\"lab-status\" data-status role=\"status\">Loading the model. Recorded evidence remains available below.</p>\n <div class=\"lab-controls\"><div><label>Choose a world<select data-preset aria-label=\"World preset\"></select></label><p data-preset-note></p><button type=\"button\" data-apply>Run these parameters →</button></div><form class=\"lab-params\" data-params aria-label=\"World parameters\"></form></div>\n <div class=\"lab-scores\"><p class=\"tiny\">Food delivered / units · higher is better</p><canvas data-curve class=\"lab-curve\" aria-label=\"Measured outcome over time for each treatment. Dashed markers identify interventions.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Treatment</th><th>At this tick</th><th>At mission end</th></tr></thead><tbody data-scores></tbody></table></div></div>\n <noscript><p>JavaScript is needed to run the simulator. Read the saved multi-seed evidence and method below.</p></noscript>\n </section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">01 / Try to break it</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Follow the trail. Then move the feast.</h2><p>Start with enough food. Compare local memory with fading traces. Now choose “The feast moves” and watch what happens when a useful memory outlives the thing it remembers. A dense cluster can be wasted motion.</p><blockquote class=\"lab-hypothesis\">When does local signaling earn its energy cost?</blockquote></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">02 / The mechanism</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>What the little world actually does.</h2><p>Every body can sense nearby food, collide with the same walls, and spend a finite energy supply. Carrying slows movement. Patches deplete when visited; food counts only when it reaches the nest. Traces persist in the environment and decay. The pooled controller can coordinate only observations its own bodies have collected.</p><p>This closes the gap between a search toy and a foraging mission. Information has a location, a lifetime and a price. Increasing population also increases the budget; the population slider is a scaling experiment, not proof that many small brains beat one large brain.</p><p lang=\"zh-Hans\" class=\"lab-zh\">每个个体都要找到食物、搬回巢穴并支付能量。踪迹会衰减，食物会耗尽，拥挤也会拖慢队伍。请比较同一种子，尤其留意过期信息何时开始帮倒忙。</p></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">03 / Recorded evidence</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Keep the inconvenient outcomes.</h2><p><strong>The simplest trace rule failed this test. Across 24 abundant worlds, local memory returned 57.54 food units on average; fading traces returned 39.79. Pooling observations returned more food, but in the hazard regime it also lost 33 of 40 bodies on average. More coordination can mean more exposure.</strong></p><p>Traces may improve discovery reuse, but stale signals, crowding, and scarcity can erase that gain.</p><p class=\"small\">24 paired seeds in each predeclared regime. Intervals are 2,000 resamples of paired primary-outcome differences. Null values are excluded from numeric aggregates and retain explicit valid counts. No biological or physical validation is implied.</p><details class=\"lab-batch\"><summary>Inspect every world and treatment</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><caption class=\"tiny\">Food delivered · mean by predeclared world</caption><thead><tr><th>World / treatment</th><th>Mean units</th><th>n</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Enough for everyone / Independent wander</th><td>50.88</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Enough for everyone / Local memory</th><td>57.54</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Enough for everyone / Fading local traces</th><td>39.79</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Enough for everyone / Pooled observations</th><td>69.33</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The last crumbs / Independent wander</th><td>17.21</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The last crumbs / Local memory</th><td>17.5</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The last crumbs / Fading local traces</th><td>7.42</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The last crumbs / Pooled observations</th><td>18.83</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Hazard corridor / Independent wander</th><td>34.33</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Hazard corridor / Local memory</th><td>35.79</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Hazard corridor / Fading local traces</th><td>26.25</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Hazard corridor / Pooled observations</th><td>38.96</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The feast moves / Independent wander</th><td>42.96</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The feast moves / Local memory</th><td>45.5</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The feast moves / Fading local traces</th><td>32.63</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The feast moves / Pooled observations</th><td>61.33</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">No trace survives / Independent wander</th><td>39.21</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">No trace survives / Local memory</th><td>43.96</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">No trace survives / Fading local traces</th><td>43.96</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">No trace survives / Pooled observations</th><td>57.5</td><td>24</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><p class=\"small\">One chosen seed is an illustration. The downloadable batch retains every world and treatment; null means unavailable. A confidence interval describes the sampled synthetic worlds, not the real world.</p><div class=\"lab-links\"><a href=\"/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/results.json\" download>All recorded runs ↓</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/README.md\">Method &amp; reproduction</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/model.mjs\">Read the model</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/source.zip\" download>Source package ↓</a></div></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section lab-method\"><p class=\"tiny\">04 / Inspect the boundary</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Enough detail to disagree.</h2><details><summary>Inputs, budgets and observation boundaries</summary><dl data-audit></dl></details><details><summary>Every measure in the current run</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\" data-summary></div></details><ul><li>Synthetic point bodies and abstract energy; not cockroach physiology.</li><li>Movement is planar; the 3D sketch is illustrative.</li><li>Agents have a nest compass and ideal self-localization. Observations of food are noisy and short range.</li><li>The central coordinator pools the same local observations with an explicit per-observation communication cost; its links are instantaneous here.</li><li>Population changes increase total bodies and energy; they are not an equal-total-budget intelligence comparison.</li></ul><p class=\"small\">3D sketching adds depth to the explanation. It does not add an unmodeled physical dimension, extra sensor data or unearned intelligence to the experiment.</p></div></section><nav class=\"lab-next\"><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/\">← Minimum Intelligence</a><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/shared-reality/\">Shared Reality →</a></nav></div>";
---
<BaseLayout title="Roach Emergence — Agent Swarm Lab — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/agent-swarm/lab.css"/>
<Fragment set:html={content}/>
<script is:inline type="module" src="/agent-swarm/client.mjs"></script>
</BaseLayout>
